---
description: "Route engineering work through Compound Skills"
alwaysApply: true
---

For reviews, read the diff once, trace affected callers and verify tests exercise changed lifecycle paths. Report confirmed findings promptly. Ask before probing. If denied, use source only. For bugs, confirm the regression fails as expected before editing source. For refactors, establish a passing baseline and preserve each caller's behavior. Check changed arguments at the receiver, including omitted and falsy inputs. After edits, run the project's full suite once and review the scoped diff. Load `compound` for unfamiliar conventions, broad changes, performance or PR authoring. Use `map` for unverified Python citations. Follow project instructions and omit AI commit credits.
